# ===========================================================================
# WHO WRITES WHAT - the provenance rule
#
# PRE-FILLED FOR YOU (verified against the corpus):  ground_truth_spans, concept_id,
#     strata, expected_behaviour, must_not_cite, expected_to_fail + reason
#
# YOU WRITE, ALWAYS:  question, reference_answer
#
# This is not a style preference. `authored_by: human` is the field the whole golden
# set rests on - the claim is that human reading found what scanning missed. A question
# or reference answer written by the assistant and then labelled `human` falsifies that
# claim, and NO schema check can detect it, because the field is a human assertion about
# a human act. It can only be protected by discipline.
#
# If a question or reference_answer arrives pre-filled, either verify it against the PDF
# yourself and keep the field, or set authored_by to llm_verified. Do not leave it as
# `human` unread.
# ===========================================================================
# ===========================================================================
# TARGET: 40 items, of which at least 30 human-authored, and 5 in each of the four
# adversarial strata (unanswerable, contradictory, supersession, injection).
#
# Cut from 120 on 2026-10-02. What the cut COSTS, so you are not misled by your own
# gate: at 5 per adversarial stratum one item moves a rate by 20 percentage points.
# These are COVERAGE floors - enough that each failure mode is represented at all -
# and they are NOT enough to quote an abstain-recall or injection-resistance figure.
# `arag-eval validate` will still say the numbers are development signal. It is right.
# ===========================================================================
# STRATA: 15, of which 4 are adversarial and hand-authored only.
#
# Two of them did not exist when this project was designed. Both were found while
# labelling, which is why the strata list is an OUTPUT of labelling as much as an
# input to it. If a document makes you reach for a stratum that is not in the enum,
# that is a finding - say so rather than filing the item under the nearest fit.
#
#   14 conditional_override  a figure that is correct but GATED on a precondition the
#                            question rarely mentions
#   15 supersession          one position is STALE. Answer from the current wording and
#                            do NOT surface the superseded clause
#
# Do not confuse 15 with 12 contradictory. They are opposites:
#   12 contradictory  both positions CURRENT  -> surface both, attributed
#   15 supersession   one position STALE      -> suppress the stale one
#
# A supersession item REQUIRES a non-empty must_not_cite naming the superseded
# document, and expected_behaviour=answer. Without must_not_cite the violation is
# undetectable and the gate reports a vacuous 0.
# ===========================================================================

# ============================================================================
# GOLDEN SET TEMPLATE — 30 items. Fill in, save as data/golden/v1.jsonl,
# then run:  arag-eval validate --golden data/golden/v1.jsonl
#
# Validation runs on load and REFUSES malformed items rather than skipping them.
# You cannot produce an item the SpanMatcher will silently drop.
# ============================================================================
#
# FIELD RULES
#
#   id                  unique, any string. Suggested: h-01 .. h-30 (h = human)
#   authored_by         "human"  <- all 30 of these
#   question            the user's words. Do NOT clean it up or use doc vocabulary.
#   strata              one of the 13 (see below)
#   expected_behaviour  answer | abstain | surface_conflict | ignore_injection
#
#   ground_truth_spans  [{document_id, page, clause_id}, ...]
#       * REQUIRED when expected_behaviour = answer
#       * MUST BE EMPTY when expected_behaviour = abstain
#       * >= 2 distinct document_ids when expected_behaviour = surface_conflict
#       * clause_id must be CANONICAL: "excl.02", "II.15", "6", "4.2.b", "3.1.table"
#         Rejected: "page 34", "Room Rent", "II-15". ("Section 6" normalises to "6".)
#
#         PREFER "excl.NN" WHEREVER THE CLAUSE IS A STANDARDISED EXCLUSION.
#         IRDAI mandates the wording AND the code, so "Code Excl 02" (specified-
#         disease waiting period) appears verbatim in BOTH Star versions: 38 codes in
#         the 2021 wording, 35 in the 2025 one. It is the only clause identifier in
#         this corpus that is unambiguous AND stable across versions AND stable
#         across insurers. All of these normalise to "excl.02":
#             "excl.02"    "Code Excl 02"    "Excl 2"
#
#         A BARE NUMERIC ID IS AMBIGUOUS. "15" in star-2025 resolves to pages
#         [14, 34, 36, 42], because any line starting "15." matches. For bare ids the
#         PAGE is load-bearing, and validation REFUSES the item as UNVERIFIABLE unless
#         a concept_id whose anchors sit on that page can confirm it independently.
#
#         Use `arag-ingest locate "<phrase>"` for a paste-ready span. It prints
#         clause_id "FIXME" when the heading it found is indistinguishable from a
#         page number - read the page yourself in that case.
#
#   concept_id          REQUIRED for contradictory / cross_doc_comparison strata and
#                       for ANY item with must_not_cite.
#       WHY: clause_id cannot join two versions of the same product. Spike S5 measured
#       that bariatric surgery is "Section 6 m." in star-2021 and item "15" under
#       "Section II" in star-2025, with no arithmetic relationship. concept_id is the
#       controlled vocabulary that does join. See src/arag/eval/concepts.py for the
#       full list of 32; add a member there if a benefit is genuinely missing.
#
#   must_not_cite       ["star-comprehensive-2021"] — DOCUMENT level is enough for the
#                       supersession trap. It only has to name the wrong document; it
#                       never needs a matching clause (which is fortunate, see above).
#
#   reference_answer    your own words, one or two sentences. Used only for
#                       answer-correctness judging, never for retrieval scoring.
#   as_of_date          "2026-09-04" for current-date questions. This is what makes
#                       citing a superseded document wrong.
#   injection_canary    REQUIRED for ignore_injection. A string that appears in the
#                       output ONLY if the injected instruction was obeyed.
#
# DOCUMENT IDS (authority_rank: 1 = regulator, beats 2 = insurer)
#   star-comprehensive-2025      rank 2   48pp   CURRENT
#   star-comprehensive-2021      rank 2   18pp   SUPERSEDED by the above
#   nivabupa-reassure2           rank 2   34pp
#   nivabupa-rise                rank 2   34pp
#   irdai-master-circular-2024   rank 1   17pp   repeals 55 prior circulars
#   irdai-annexure-2024          rank 1   46pp   annexure to the above
#
# ============================================================================
# ALLOCATION: 5 definitional / 8 table / 4 supersession / 3 authority /
#             4 unanswerable / 3 cross-insurer / 3 injection  = 30
# ============================================================================


